{
  "info": {
    "name": "smtp4dev Mock API v3.8.6",
    "description": "Test collection for the mock smtp4dev service. Base URL defaults to http://localhost:8124. In docker-compose, the service is reachable at http://smtp4dev-api:8124.\n\nsmtp4dev is a .NET application and every contract shows it. **Pages, not offsets**: each list is a `PagedResult` with `results`, `firstRowOnPage`, `lastRowOnPage`, `currentPage`, `pageCount`, `pageSize` and `rowCount`, driven by `page` (1-based), `pageSize`, `sortColumn` and `sortIsDescending`. **Sessions are first-class and separate from messages**: a session is the SMTP conversation kept with its full transcript, including the ones that produced no message because the client failed to authenticate or hung up after a rejected recipient. **Mailboxes are recipient-matching rules**, with `Default` as the catch-all -- smtp4dev *routes* to a mailbox where Inbucket *derives* one. **MIME parts are a tree** addressed by section number (`1`, `1.1`, `1.1.2`), and a container part has children rather than content. **The server settings are writable**: `POST /api/Server` is the Settings dialog, and lowering `numberOfMessagesToKeep` trims the store on the spot.\n\nThe delete-everything routes really are spelled with a literal `*`.\n\nOne endpoint is marked in its own response as a mock addition: `POST /api/Messages` stands in for the SMTP delivery a mock cannot accept. Requests labelled '(N expected)' assert an error path.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
